course: dictionary
lesson: 9700
title: Suitable for whom?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Suitable means right or good for a person, a purpose or a situation. «Suitable clothes for the rain» are clothes that keep you dry. Clothes for a snowy day might not be suitable for a summer picnic. Always ask: suitable for whom, or for what?
explain: «The number on a game box is an age rating: it says who the game is suitable for, not how long or hard it is.» So a rating tells you the right audience, not the difficulty. Look for the words «suitable for» to find out who something fits.
explain: A rating tells you what is suitable, not how something will make you feel. «A U or G film can still be sad or a little scary.» So a suitable film can still upset you, and if it does, you can choose another one that suits you better.
fact: Suitable means right or good for a person, a purpose or a situation.
fact: «Suitable for» tells you who or what something fits.
fact: «Not suitable for children» means it is not right for young people to see or play.
fact: In the UK, the watershed is 9 pm: programmes not suitable for children are not shown on ordinary TV channels before then.
fact: In the USA and Canada, games are rated by the ESRB; «M» means Mature, suitable for about 17 and up.
exercise: «The number on a game box is an age rating: it says who the game is suitable for.» What does suitable mean here? | Very long | Loud and busy | *Right or good for a certain person | Very hard to play
exercise: In maths, «choose a suitable unit» to measure a pencil. Which unit is suitable? | Kilometres | *Centimetres | Litres | Tonnes
exercise: Which phrase means right for young people to see or play? | A suitable time to stop | Suitable for everyone in the world | *Not suitable for children | Suitable clothes
test: Mum says the game is not suitable for your little brother. What does she mean? | It is too short for him | It is great for every age | It is too cheap to buy | *It is not right for a young child
test: In the USA and Canada, roughly what age is an «M» game suitable for? | About 5 and up | *About 17 and up | About 9 pm and later | About 10 and under
exam: Why might a «U» or «G» film still upset you? | The rating is always wrong and should be ignored | *A rating says what is suitable, not how a film will make you feel | Ratings show the price of the ticket | Films are only sad when they are very long
